\sqrt{\cos^2 7 \theta} &= \sqrt{4 \cos^4 \theta} \\
\left| \cos 7 \theta \right| &= 2 \left| \cos \theta \right|^2 \\
\cos 7 \theta &= \pm 2 \cos^2 \theta \\
\cos 7 \theta - 2 \cos^2 \theta &= 0
\end{align*}

In order to solve the quadratic equation, we can complete the square:

